bug_report:
[14 Regression] The vectorizer is introducing out-of-bounds memory access
The following function is miscompiled for x86_64 when compiled with
-O3 -march=x86-64-v2


unsigned long
foo (const char *s, unsigned long n)
{
 unsigned long len = 0;
 while (*s++ && n--)
   ++len;
 return len;
}


The original function reads two bytes from 's' when called as:

 char a[4];
 a[0] = 1;
 a[1] = 0;
 foo(a, 1000);

However, the vectorized function reads 16 bytes (thereby accessing the buffer out of bounds) as it reads one vector at a time when s[0] != 0 and n >= 16.
